# L §8.1 'It carries' (round 8b): a read whose key is a hole reads no cell, so it carries the key's questions only, as
# a band read at a hole x does (§5.9). k has no row, so it is HOLE-UNGOVERNED with its question 'which era?'; x[k]
# reads no cell of x, so v carries 'which era?' and not x's question 'x?' (x[new] has no row either); so does y[k],
# a def read at the hole key; q3 adds x[new], a cell that is read, with its question 'x?'.
=== m.tally
model p16
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

index era = [old, new]

input k: key era question "which era?"
input x[r in era]: num question "x?"

def v: num = x[k] at reader
def y[r in era]: num = x[r] at reader

ask q: v law 2026-06-30
ask q2: y[k] law 2026-06-30
ask q3: x[k] + x[new] law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x[old] = 1
=== expect
q: ?"which era?" (k)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
q2: ?"which era?" (k)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
q3: ?"which era?" (k) ?"x?" (x[new])
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
